/*
  Localizable.strings (hu)
  AstroTool

  The V2 UI's Hungarian translation table. SwiftUI's `Text("literal")`,
  `Button`, `Label`, `Toggle`, `Picker`, `TableColumn`, `.help()`,
  `.accessibilityLabel()` and `.navigationTitle()` all resolve their
  `LocalizedStringKey` against `Bundle.main` -- the app target's bundle, not
  AstroUI's library bundle -- at render time. Putting this table here
  therefore localizes every one of those call sites in AstroUI with zero
  call-site changes. The key is always the exact English literal; a key
  with no entry here falls back to that literal, so English needs no file
  of its own.

  Keep this reproducible: `scripts/extract-localizable-strings.swift`
  extracts every literal that needs an entry, and
  `Tests/AstroUITests/LocalizationCoverageTests.swift` fails the build if a
  key is missing one -- except for the allowlist of brand/domain terms that
  intentionally stay in English (see that test file for the list).
*/

"System" = "Rendszer szerint";
"Hungarian" = "Magyar";
"English" = "Angol";
"Language" = "Nyelv";
"Changing the language takes effect the next time you restart AstroTool -- it does not apply immediately." = "A nyelv módosítása csak az AstroTool következő újraindításakor lép életbe -- nem azonnal.";
